WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.164 --> 00:00:10.364
In tutorial 6.3, you'll finish
a page that needs your edits,

00:00:10.414 --> 00:00:11.948
and get it ready to publish.

00:00:12.969 --> 00:00:15.629
First, open Content. On the board,

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:19.729
a page that needs your edits says
Needs your edits, and Not ready.

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:22.241
Click See what to edit to open its report.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:28.285
The report says why the page is not ready
yet: 2 details are still in brackets,

00:00:28.335 --> 00:00:30.794
like the number of support
agents in the pilot.

00:00:32.256 --> 00:00:34.691
Further down, What you do says it plainly:

00:00:34.741 --> 00:00:37.713
fill in or delete each
bracket in the editor.

00:00:39.235 --> 00:00:44.468
Until then, approval stays closed, so a
page with blanks can't go live by mistake.

00:00:46.231 --> 00:00:51.506
Click Open the editor. Find each bracket,
and type the real detail in its place,

00:00:51.556 --> 00:00:54.666
like 12 agents, or a hospitality client.

00:00:56.235 --> 00:00:59.210
Then save your version.
It's checked right away,

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:02.898
and Your version passed the check
means nothing stops the page any more.

00:01:04.756 --> 00:01:09.096
Finally, click Make the final
version. Your edits go into the page,

00:01:09.146 --> 00:01:12.078
and the whole page is checked
again before you approve it.

00:01:13.756 --> 00:01:17.496
So the page you publish carries
your real details, not a blank.

00:01:19.281 --> 00:01:24.206
So, to recap: open the page that
needs edits, see what to edit and why,

00:01:24.256 --> 00:01:27.444
fill the brackets in the editor,
and make the final version.

00:01:28.427 --> 00:01:33.177
Your draft is ready to go live. Next,
check any page before you publish it,

00:01:33.227 --> 00:01:35.090
in tutorial 6.4.
